        "unit_type": "prose",
        "text": "THESE MONSTROUS RATS, WARPED BY YEARS OF EXPOSURE TO TOXIC WASTE, HAVE DEVELOPED A SICKLY, HAIRLESS HIDE AND ARE PERPETUALLY DRENCHED IN A NOXIOUS, GOOEY SECRETION. KNOWN AS FLESH RATS, THESE VERMIN SKULK IN SEWER SYSTEMS, THEIR BODIES PULSING AND SEEPING WITH CAUSTIC ICHOR THAT BURNS EVERYTHING IT TOUCHES. DESPITE THEIR HORRIFIC APPEARANCE, THEY REMAIN NIMBLE AND QUICK, DARTING IN AND OUT OF SHADOWS TO SCRAPE BY ON WHATEVER SCRAPS THEY CAN FIND, OR ELSE FEED ON THOSE UNFORTUNATE ENOUGH TO STUMBLE UPON THEM.\nArmor Class : 12\nHit Points: 5 Hit Dice : 1d8+1\nSpeed: walk : 30",
